+## TL;DR
+- `s-4-m-a-n/RestaurantBot` is one of the clearest open restaurant-ordering chatbot examples built with Rasa, Flask, and Docker.
+- `theognis1002/ocr-restaurant-menu-import`, `AlexBandurin/Menu_Reader`, and `dieharders/ai-menu-generator` are the most directly useful menu-ingestion repos.
+- Yelp-based recommendation projects are the deepest category on GitHub for restaurant AI; this list includes 10 verified options.
+- Forecasting coverage exists, but it is thinner and more academic than ordering and recommendation. Restaurants needing production demand planning will likely combine these repos with their own data pipeline.
+- A few GitHub pages did not expose an exact last-commit date in cached HTML; those cases are called out honestly instead of guessed.
+
+## Why This List
+Open source matters for restaurant AI because margins are tight, workflows are operationally messy, and vendor lock-in is expensive. The best AI tools for restaurants in 2026 are not just flashy demos: they need inspectable code, adaptable prompts or models, clear licenses, and a GitHub repo that shows real implementation details. This list intentionally excludes closed SaaS products and only includes repositories with public `github.com` URLs.
