+#### [OCR Image Menu Text Extractor](https://github.com/theognis1002/ocr-restaurant-menu-import)
+> **Description:** This repo is narrowly useful for restaurant operations: it extracts text from menu images with `pytesseract`, then uses an LLM via `litellm` to structure that text into JSON. The README is implementation-oriented, covering multiprocessing, image-format support, configuration, and a simple `main.py` workflow that outputs machine-readable menu data. That makes it a strong building block for digital menu migration, menu QA, or syncing printed menus into POS-adjacent systems. GitHub shows a Python codebase, an MIT license, and a public repo; the static snapshot did not expose stars or the exact last-commit date.
