+#### [Menu_Reader](https://github.com/AlexBandurin/Menu_Reader)
+> **Description:** `Menu_Reader` turns a restaurant-menu image into OCR text, then runs ML classification and NLP steps to identify actual menu items and sort them into categories. The README is unusually specific: it documents feature engineering on 2,500+ OCR rows, compares Decision Tree, Random Forest, and XGBoost, and uses BERT-based categorization plus Azure Functions to offload heavier processing. GitHub shows 18 stars, Jupyter Notebook as the primary language, no license listed on the repo page, and 27 commits; the exact last-commit date was not surfaced in cached HTML.
