+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for restaurants in 2026?
+The strongest open source options on GitHub right now cluster around four use cases: menu OCR, ordering assistants, recommendation engines, and review or demand analytics. For the most restaurant-specific repos, start with `RestaurantBot`, `OCR Image Menu Text Extractor`, `Menu_Reader`, and the Yelp-based recommendation projects.
+
+### Are there fully self-hosted AI tools for restaurant ordering?
+Yes, but most are starter projects rather than mature platforms. `RestaurantBot` is the clearest self-hosted example here because it uses Rasa, Flask, and Docker. `restaurant_order_bot` is also useful, but it is closer to a minimal prototype.
+
+### Which open source repos help convert printed menus into structured data?
+The best matches in this list are `ocr-restaurant-menu-import`, `Menu_Reader`, and `ai-menu-generator`. These focus on OCR, menu-item extraction, category labeling, translations, or interactive digital menu generation.
+
+### Are there open source AI tools for restaurant recommendation engines?
+Yes. This is the deepest category on GitHub. Yelp-based repos such as `Restaurant-Recommendation-System-using-Yelp-Dataset`, `Hybrid-Restaurant-Recommender`, and `Restaurant-Recommendation` are strong starting points for search, ranking, and discovery features.
+
+### Can restaurants use open source AI for review sentiment analysis and fake-review detection?
+Yes. Repos like `Restaurant-Review-Scraping-and-Sentiment-Analysis`, `Yelp_Sentiment_Analysis`, `ASAP`, and the two Yelp fake-review projects are all relevant for review intelligence, guest-feedback clustering, and trust-and-safety workflows.
+
+### Are there open source AI repos for restaurant demand forecasting and revenue prediction?
+There are some, but this is still a thinner category than recommendation or chatbots. `Food-Demand-Forecasting`, `food-stock-demand-forecast`, `restaurant_sales_forecasting`, and the revenue-prediction repos are useful references, though most teams will need to adapt them to their own POS and inventory data.
+
